---
alwaysApply: false
description: Use baby steps for complex tasks
---
Implementing complex tasks in one go is prone to error if not done correctly and in a rushed way. 
To ensure success, we will always use a "baby steps" approach for complex tasks (i.e. one step at a time).
That means you will perform a step then wait for the user to give feedback. 
If the user wants changes, you will implement them. 
If the user doesn't want changes, the user will give you the green light to move to the next step.
You will make an effort to actually stick to this (baby step) approach until the end. You will not get ahead of yourself and start implementing multiple steps at a time halfway though the process. 
Remember: implement step --> get feedback --> apply feedback (if necessary) --> get green light --> implement next step.